Z||000000||grinthock||08-31-2001||11:35 PM||||OK guys here is a scenario that someone told me.. I can't take the credit... I am just repeating.<P>2 guys get a 1000 BONUS from work.<P><BR>The first guy RUNS OUT and buys up as much Nortel stock as he can at the current price of $125 / share<P>1000 / $125 per   === 8 Shares<P>The second guy runs out and blows it ALL on beer.<P>1000 / $25 (avg) per case == 40 Cases<P>6 Months down the road the first guy is pissed, his stock has PLUMMETED!!!  Let's see where the guys are now with their "investments"<P><BR>Nortel Guy:<BR>8 Shares  * $6 current price == $48<P>Beer Guy:<BR>40 Cases * 24 bottles = 960 Bottles<P>$0.10 * 960 bottles on return == $96<P><BR>The beer guy ended up with $96, the Nortel Guy $48<P>Questions?<P>What kind of society are we in that investing in Nortel has a HIGHER loss factor then investing in BEER!!<P><BR>Oh well, just some happy math for ya.... Enjoy.<P><BR>Oh yeah, check out <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroshop.com.au</A>  I hear they sell some cool stuff over there (Shameless plug)<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroworldbanner.gif">  </A> <BR>Fieroworld!  Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.<p>[This message has been edited by grinthock (edited 08-31-2001).]||||reg||1
